    "body": "Review blocker fixed (cf6c958d, with main merged):\n- **Guards:** Haas, Mazak and Sinumerik now define `onProbeGuard` (#174's protected positioning moves).\n  - Haas: `G31` + `IF[ABS[#506x-t]GT0.001]THEN#3000=3`.\n  - Mazak: `G31` + the IF…GOTO form.\n  - Sinumerik: `MEAS=1 G1` + `IF ==1` → `MSG`/`SETAL(65002)`/`M0`, chosen over ``, which keeps a stale value after a clear move.\n  - Each guard alarm is distinct from no-contact and out-of-tolerance.\n- **Bug fixed along the way:** a negative target gave a doubled sign (`#5061--7`); Haas and Mazak now use fanuc's `minusU` helper.\n- **Goldens:** only the 2 guard moves changed in each dialect's `probe_bore_centre.nc`; the Mazak and Sinumerik label/N renumbering is explained.\n- **Tests:** a new guard test per dialect; probe_dialects passes 13/13, as do probe_op, probe_guard, conformance, posting, probe_pick, probe_reach, inverted_probe, the post suites and camcraft-post. Clippy is clean.\n- **Heidenhain:** stays a named refusal, so this is now `Refs #173`. Follow-up filed as https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/628.\n- **For the maintainer:** none of these controls is available to the contributor, so there is no real-control run; it is verified only by tests and goldens.",
